    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's intense, i like it. one thing though... some people argue that if every candidate is terrible, the most \"moral\" thing to do is actually to abstain as a form of protest, or that forcing people to vote is just a way to legitimize a broken system. how can we write the speech to shut down that argument? i want to show that their \"protest\" is actually just an excuse for laziness and that the only real moral path is to vote. can you add a section that addresses and basically dismantles that \"protest\" argument?",
