      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To those who cry \"protest\" through absence, I say their silence is merely the loudest excuse for cowardice. Claiming to protest by staying home is a convenient abdication of your duty, a passive gesture that accomplishes nothing. True moral protest is exerted in the ballot box, where you force a reckoning, not in the shadows of apathy. We do not need flawless candidates to vote; we need engaged citizens strong enough to relentlessly demand better from the ones who do run. Participation is the active refusal to accept the mediocre, and that refusal must be visible.",
